[heading]About this mod[/heading]

[b]Travel Between Visited Traders[/b] adds a trader dialog option that lets you travel back to traders you have already visited.

Talk to a trader once to record that trader for the current save. After that, use [b]Travel to a visited trader[/b] in trader dialog and pick a destination from the list.

For normal single-player use, install the mod and leave the default settings alone.

[line]

[heading]Main features[/heading]

[list]
[*]Travel between traders you have already visited
[*]Destination list shows trader name, distance, direction, coordinates, current access mode, and any configured travel cost
[*]Mode and page status are kept separate from selectable destination choices
[*]Full-screen trader-transport overlay while travel is preparing and in progress, with clearer departure and arrival messages
[*]Optional distance-based travel costs, with gas as the default cost item when enabled
[*]Long destination lists use pages so every visited trader remains reachable
[*]Known vanilla and Wasteland Mod trader names display cleanly when recognized
[*]Supports English and Japanese
[*]Works in single-player and multiplayer
[*]Includes Personal, Party, and Shared access modes for servers
[*]Keeps older visited-trader save data readable
[*]Reduces duplicate destinations from older records and repeat visits to the same trader
[*]Prepares distant or unloaded trader areas before travel, and cancels the teleport if the destination is not ready
[/list]

[line]

[heading]Installation[/heading]

Extract the [b]VisitedTraderTeleport[/b] folder into:

[quote]
7 Days To Die\Mods\VisitedTraderTeleport
[/quote]

The mod requires the vanilla [b]0_TFP_Harmony[/b] mod that ships with current 7 Days to Die versions.

[b]Anti-cheat should be disabled for this DLL mod.[/b]

[line]

[heading]Single-player[/heading]

No configuration is needed for normal single-player play.

The default mode is [b]Personal[/b], which means you can travel only to traders you have personally visited in that save.

Travel is free by default. The short visible transport transition is enabled by default.

[line]

[heading]Multiplayer[/heading]

Install the mod on both the server and every client.

In multiplayer, the server controls trader access, travel cost, and teleport validation. Clients show the destination list allowed by the server.

The config is loaded from the installed mod folder beside [b]VisitedTraderTeleport.dll[/b], so custom folder names work as long as the [b]Config[/b] folder stays with the mod.

[line]

[heading]Access modes[/heading]

[b]Personal[/b]
Each player can travel only to traders they personally visited.

[b]Party[/b]
Players can travel to traders visited by themselves or by their current party members.

[b]Shared[/b]
Any trader visited by anyone in the active server/save data becomes available to everyone.

[line]

[heading]Configuration[/heading]

For multiplayer, change settings on the server:

[quote]
7 Days To Die\Mods\VisitedTraderTeleport\Config\VisitedTraderTeleport.xml
[/quote]

Access mode:

[quote]
<AccessMode value="personal" />
[/quote]

Use [b]personal[/b], [b]party[/b], or [b]shared[/b].

Optional travel cost:

[quote]
<TravelCost enabled="false" item="ammoGasCan" displayName="gas" perMeter="0.1" minimum="0" />
[/quote]

Set [b]enabled[/b] to [b]true[/b] to charge for travel. The default item is vanilla gas. New configs can use [b]perMeter[/b] for finer tuning; older [b]perKilometer[/b] configs still work.

To charge Duke's casino tokens instead of gas:

[quote]
<TravelCost enabled="true" item="casinoCoin" displayName="Dukes" perMeter="1" minimum="0" />
[/quote]

Travel transition:

[quote]
<TravelTransition enabled="true" durationSeconds="5" disableCamera="false" sound="suv_startup" />
[/quote]

Restart the dedicated server, host process, or single-player game after changing the config.

[line]

[heading]Upgrading from older versions[/heading]

[b]You do not need to reset your save when upgrading.[/b]

Older versions stored visited trader data in [b]VisitedTraderTeleportVisited.txt[/b]. Newer versions use [b]VisitedTraderTeleportData.json[/b].

The old TXT data still loads for compatibility, and new visits are written to the newer JSON file. Existing data is not deleted during upgrade.

When old or duplicate records are found, the mod may tidy them automatically while keeping visited-trader ownership linked to the matching trader records. A one-time backup named [b]VisitedTraderTeleportData.before-0.4.16.json[/b] is created before automatic JSON normalization.

For extra safety before updating a server, stop the server and copy [b]VisitedTraderTeleportData.json[/b] and [b]VisitedTraderTeleportVisited.txt[/b] from the save folder first.

Dedicated servers read legacy data from the machine that owns the active save. Old TXT files that exist only on former clients are not transferred automatically.

[line]

[heading]Notes[/heading]

[list]
[*]The current trader is not shown as a destination
[*]Long destination lists show page controls inside the trader dialog
[*]If there are no valid destinations, the destination screen explains that none are available in the current mode
[*]Teleport destinations are based on the position saved when the trader visit was recorded
[*]If a destination cannot be prepared in time, travel is cancelled instead of forcing the player into an unsafe area
[*]After multiplayer travel, the client refreshes destination visuals to reduce transparent POI objects
[/list]
